<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <%
        const pageTitle = 'Mii File Format Guide - InfiniMii';
        const pageDesc = 'Reference guide to common Mii file formats, QR workflows, compatibility notes, and which InfiniMii tools to use for each format.';
        const canonicalUrl = `${baseUrl}/guides/formats`;
        const keywords = 'mii file formats, mii format guide, wii mii file, 3ds mii format, switch mii data, mii qr format';
        const breadcrumbs = [
            { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
            { name: 'Mii Format Guide', url: '/guides/formats' }
        ];
        const schemaType = 'TechArticle';
        %>
        <%- include('metaTags', { title: pageTitle, description: pageDesc, canonicalUrl, keywords }) %>
        <%- include('structuredData') %>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/global.css">
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/utilityPages.css">
    </head>
    <body>
        <%- include('globalStyle') %>
        <%- include('header') %>
        <%- include('accountDisplay') %>
        <main class="content faq-content" role="main">
            <%- include('sidebar') %>
            <article class="faq-article">
                <h1>Mii File Format Guide</h1>
                <p class="faq-lede">A quick reference for the Mii formats you will run into on InfiniMii, what each one is for, and which tool to use next.</p>

                <nav class="faq-nav" aria-label="Format Guide Sections">
                    <h2>Browse This Guide</h2>
                    <ul class="faq-nav-list">
                        <li><a href="#formats">Common Mii Formats</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#tools">Which Tool Should You Use?</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#compatibility">Compatibility Notes</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </nav>

                <section id="formats" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Common Mii Formats</h2>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Wii-era formats:</strong> <code>RCD</code> and <code>RSD</code> are classic Mii exports used by Wii-era workflows. You'll also run into <code>MII</code>, <code>MIIGX</code>, <code>MAE</code>, and others. These are all just different names of <code>RCD</code> born primarily out of split reverse engineering efforts. <code>RCD/RSD</code> are the official formats as named by Nintendo in their files.</li>
                            <li><strong>3DS and Wii U formats:</strong> <code>CFCD</code>, <code>CFSD</code>, <code>FFCD</code>, and <code>FFSD</code> store richer Mii data and often pair with QR workflows. <code>CFED/FFED</code> are unofficial terms to represent the standard encryption used on these codes for QR purposes. <code>PNG, JPG, and other Image formats</code> can be used to hold QR codes that most Mii tools, the 3DS, and the Wii U can scan.</li>
                            <li><strong>QR exports:</strong> Use <code>qr</code> when you need a scannable code for compatible systems like 3DS and Wii U.</li>
                            <li><strong>Modern formats:</strong> <code>NFCD</code>, <code>NFSD</code>, and <code>charinfo</code> cover newer Nintendo Mii data workflows.</li>
                            <li><strong>My Nintendo Mii Studio:</strong> <code>MNMS</code> is the format used in localstorage on the Mii Studio website. You can copy this type as hex to use with most importer/exporter tools.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section id="tools" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Which Tool Should You Use?</h2>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <ul>
                            <li><a href="/convert">Converter</a> when you already have Mii data and need a new output format.</li>
                            <li><a href="/qr">QR Scanner</a> when you are starting from a QR image.</li>
                            <li><a href="/guides/transfer">Transfer Guide</a> when the best method depends on the source and destination hardware.</li>
                            <li><a href="/amiibo">Amiibo Tools</a> or <a href="/wiimote">Wii Remote Tools</a> when your Mii lives inside those specific devices.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p><a href="/convert" class="cta-link">Open the converter</a></p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section id="compatibility" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Compatibility Notes</h2>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <ul>
                            <li>Older Nintendo systems support fewer facial features than newer ones, so down-level conversions can simplify details.</li>
                            <li>QR code workflows are especially useful for 3DS and Wii U transfers.</li>
                            <li>Switch-related transfers often rely on manual recreation or Amiibo instead of direct file import.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </article>
            <%- include('featuredMiis') %>
        </main>
        <%- include('footer') %>
    </body>
</html>
